values ('flatiron-institute-polymathic-ai-research-internship-in-ai-for-physics', 'Flatiron Institute, Polymathic AI', 'Research Internship in AI for Physics', 'Research Internship in AI for Physics', 'academic_lab', 'New York', 'United States', 'onsite', null, 'Flexible, around April to September 2027', 'yes', '5 to 6 months', 'closed', 'Strong background in machine learning and/or applied mathematics; interest in physics and scientific applications; Python and PyTorch', 'yes', null, null, 'email', null, null, 'mailing_list', null, 'Developing and understanding foundation models trained across many physical systems: multiscale models, generalization across systems, learning from partially observed data, and interactions between LLMs and scientific models.', 'Apply with a CV and a brief description of research interests. Stated as compatible with the MVA internship. Supervisor offers support for a separate application to the NYU Center for Data Science PhD (fall 2027, deadline around 03/12/2026, fully funded). The offer says nothing about stipend or US visa (J-1). Shared through the MVA group on 01/10/2026. Apply by email to the address given in the posting.', array['physics-sim', 'foundation-models']::text[], null, null, 5, 6, '2026-10-02', '2026-11-01', '2026-11-06', current_date)
